# Apixaban + 10 H2O: cheap XTB2 pre-equilibration MD, WITH spherical confinement
# Purpose:
#   The first attempt at this pre-equilibration (Apixaban_10H2O_XTB_preequil.inp,
#   no confinement) failed: over 20 ps, 7 of 10 waters flew away to 90-310 Angstrom
#   from Apixaban (no periodic boundary conditions / no wall -> unconfined gas-phase
#   MD disperses weakly-bound solvent instead of clustering it).
#
#   This version adds a "Cell Sphere" - a soft, non-periodic repulsive wall (NOT a
#   pulling/biasing force) centered on the Apixaban centroid. It only pushes back
#   atoms that try to leave the sphere; inside the sphere, dynamics are completely
#   unbiased. This prevents evaporation while still allowing the waters to freely
#   explore positions around Apixaban and find H-bonding sites.
#
# Sphere center = centroid of the 59 Apixaban heavy+H atoms in the initial structure
#   (31.537, -19.865, -0.109), computed from Apixaban_Explicit10H2O_repositioned_initial.xyz
# Sphere radius = 14.0 Angstrom (Apixaban's own farthest atom from this centroid is
#   ~9.0 Angstrom, so this gives roughly a 5 Angstrom solvation shell of free space
#   beyond the Apixaban surface before the wall engages)
# Spring constant = 20 kJ/mol/Ang^2 (a bit stiffer than the 10 kJ/mol/Ang^2 default,
#   still soft enough not to require a smaller time step)
#
# Starting geometry: same initial (unequilibrated) structure as before -
#   Apixaban_Explicit10H2O_repositioned_initial.xyz
#
# Note: XTB2 energies/forces are NOT at the same level as r2SCAN-3c - this run is
#   only for generating a better-equilibrated starting geometry (a late frame from
#   this trajectory, once waters have settled near Apixaban), not for any
#   energetics used in the DMSO/Water/MeOH comparison.

! XTB2 MD

%md
  Timestep 1.0_fs
  Initvel 298.15_K
  Thermostat NHC 298.15_K Timecon 20.0_fs
  Cell Sphere 31.537, -19.865, -0.109, 14.0 Spring 20
  Dump Position Stride 100 Filename "Apixaban_10H2O_XTB_preequil_confined.xyz"
  Run 20000
end

* xyzfile 0 1 Apixaban_Explicit10H2O_repositioned_initial.xyz
